# Recipe for script/combat/pvp.razor. Build it with: python3 util/build-scripts.py
# Every setting of the loop is under #@ config, grouped by the module that reads it.
# The blocks are files in module/, run in the order listed under #@ blocks.
#@ output script/combat/pvp.razor

#@ header
# Shared field PvP self-sustain: instant items first, healing agents, PvP buffs kept up, swing based weapon swap.
# Needs: the heal pot and reflect bars, and a swing N bar (WeaponSwing type) for each enabled weapon slot.
# Turn it on when a PvP fight starts. All offense stays manual: attack spells, TK, explosion potions,
# pets, targeting and melee requests. The script never cuts a manual cast or cursor.
# No start 4 lines (conventions 02.D): a manual cursor or cast held at Play is kept.
# Arm/Dress must remove conflicting equipment.
# Design and in-game checks: blueprint/pvp.html part 5.E, blueprint/open-items.html part 10.
#
# Shape
#   Each block reads the live state and acts on the spot, the way bard-necro-enhanced and
#   lumberjack-enhanced do. No block hands a decision to a later one. Item uses go through
#   Razor's object delay queue, and every block waits while that queue is busy. A cast block
#   waits out its own cast in a for 60 poll, so the next block sees casting end.
#
# Input rules (wiki Combat Overview, blueprint/pvp.html part 5.B)
#   Potions and the pouch are instant and go out while a spell is casting.
#   Drinking with a finished precast cursor in hand cancels that spell, so a potion or a
#   bandage waits while any cursor is held. Agents and buffs need no cast and no cursor.
#   Only our own buff cast is cut, at config__buff_max_loss, so the next pass can heal.
#   No walk guard (config__walk_guard 0): in a fight there is no better moment to wait for.
#
# Cost (blueprint/razor.html part 6)
#   findtype is the most expensive statement. Reagents are read in REAGENTS every
#   cooldown__reagents and right after a "More reagents are needed" refusal, and the cast
#   blocks read the flags. Potions are looked up only inside a block that already needs one.

#@ blocks
# Before the loop, then again at the top of every pass.
#@ use core/pvp-stop                                            stops inside structured PvP
# Every pass, in this order.
#@ use core/reagents                                            reagent flags for the recovery spells and the buffs
#@ use core/paralyze                                            trapped pouch while held
#@ use core/cure                                                cure potion, else the Cure agent
#@ use core/heal                                                heal potion, else Greater Heal at the emergency line
#@ use core/bandage                                             self bandage
#@ use core/light-heal                                          light Heal, the bandage stand-in
#@ use core/refresh                                             Refresh at low stamina
#@ use core/stat-potions                                        Strength, Agility and Magic Resist
#@ use core/self-buffs                                          Reactive Armor, then Magic Reflection
#@ use combat/weapon-slots                                      arms the slot whose swing is ready
#@ use core/pass-wait                                           end of the pass

#@ config
# ---- core/switches -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Independent features. No option overrides another.
@setvar! config__use_magery 1
@setvar! config__use_potions 1
@setvar! config__use_bandages 1
# 1 makes our own casts wait while the walk bar runs, so a step does not break them.
# 0 casts while walking, for a fight where there is no better moment to wait for.
# This loop: pvp casts while walking: in a fight there is no better moment to wait for.
@setvar! config__walk_guard 0
# 1 when warmode is the player's manual control window: our own casts stand down while it is on.
@setvar! config__warmode_is_manual 0

# ---- core/output -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional script overheads. Essential warnings remain visible.
@setvar! config__chatty 1
# Journal diagnostics. Each block that writes one says so in its own comments.
@setvar! config__sysmsg 1

# ---- core/cure ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Minimum current mana for the Cure agent.
@setvar! config__mana_cure 6

# ---- core/heal ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Missing hit points, not percent.
#   heal_hits       heal potion
#   emergency_hits  Greater Heal when no heal potion can go out. Not below heal_hits
@setvar! config__heal_hits 35
@setvar! config__emergency_hits 35
# Minimum current mana for Greater Heal. It keeps no reserve: raise it to 31 to always leave
# 20 mana for an attack or Teleport.
@setvar! config__mana_greater_heal 11

# ---- core/bandage ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Healing must be above this to bandage. 0 means any Healing at all.
@setvar! config__heal_skill_min 0

# ---- core/light-heal ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Light Heal beside the bandages. With no bandage able to run (use_bandages 0, no Healing, or
# none left) it goes anyway, as the bandage stand-in. Needs use_magery.
@setvar! config__use_light_heal 0
# Missing hit points that start the light Heal, and its minimum current mana.
@setvar! config__light_hits 15
@setvar! config__mana_heal 4

# ---- core/refresh ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Current stamina at or below this drinks a Refresh.
@setvar! config__refresh_stam 15

# ---- core/stat-potions -------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_stat_potions 1
@setvar! config__use_resist_potion 1
# STR and DEX with the Greater potion on: your base plus 20. Below these the potion is drunk.
# Bless and the Strength and Agility spells, ours or an ally's, show the same icons as the
# potions but add less than its 20, so the stat is what tells the potion apart.
# This loop: The loop is shared, so set these two for the character that runs it.
@setvar! config__str_potion 120
@setvar! config__dex_potion 100

# ---- core/self-buffs ---------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_reactive_armor 1
@setvar! config__use_magic_reflect 1
# Minimum current mana to start each buff.
@setvar! config__mana_reactive_armor 4
@setvar! config__mana_magic_reflect 14
# Missing hit points at which buffs are not started, and cut mid cast.
# This loop: Keep this equal to config__emergency_hits.
@setvar! config__buff_max_loss 35
# 0 keeps buffs back while poisoned and cuts one that is casting.
@setvar! config__buff_when_poisoned 1

# ---- combat/weapon-slots -----------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__use_weapon 1
# Weapon slots. Slot N reads the "swing N" bar. Graphic 0 turns the slot off.
# A slot whose swing is ready wins, 4 down to 1. With none ready and both hands empty, the
# lowest enabled slot re-arms.
@setvar! config__weapon_1_graphic 31128
@setvar! config__weapon_2_graphic 0
@setvar! config__weapon_3_graphic 0
@setvar! config__weapon_4_graphic 31190

#@ state
# pvp is always in a fight, so the stat potions are kept up the whole time.
@setvar! var__fighting 1

#@ setup
overhead "[ pvp, on ]" 290
if config__sysmsg = 1
    sysmsg "PvP sustain v9 loaded. Manual offense, recovery first." 88
endif
